  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may interact with SMMC-7721, a cancer cell line. The drug is implicated in targeting Thioredoxin, a protein involved in cellular redox regulation and apoptosis. Thioredoxin is further targeted by multiple compounds, including Isodaucene and Phorone, which in turn are linked to SMMC-7721. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may act as a modulator of Thioredoxin, potentially influencing cellular processes that are critical for cell survival and proliferation in SMMC-7721 cells.\n\nThe evidence is supported by a series of target relationships, all of which are consistent with a mechanistic pathway involving Thioredoxin and its downstream targets. The presence of multiple targets suggests that 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving redox regulation and cell death pathways. However, the exact nature of the interaction between 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone and Thioredoxin remains to be fully elucidated, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the drug's mode of action in this context.",
